MerkleAdapter report synchronization
├── anyone can synchronize an accepted report without moving funds or changing capital flow
├── anyone can stage direct returns with stale NAV while preserving earlier checkpoints
├── allocation and deallocation synchronize internally before changing capital flows
│   ├── allocation applies losses before recording new capital
│   └── deallocation releases covered staged cash and pays the requested amount
├── without an accepted report, no report is applied
├── acceptance only reads adapter flow history and does not settle liquidity or read cash
│   └── failed synchronization leaves adapter state unchanged and can be retried
├── rejected reports cannot release cash; curator acceptance still requires synchronization
├── repeat synchronization cannot restore paid liquidity or cap a new request
├── expired reports or NAV arithmetic overflow revert synchronization atomically
│   └── requests and pulls remain available to stage recovery cash
├── delayed synchronization uses the latest accepted report and current NAV
└── all arrivals staged through the snapshot are released together
